    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="summary">
    <h2>Lesson Summary</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>National income measures the total income generated from production.</li>
      <li>Nominal income is measured in current money terms.</li>
      <li>Real income is adjusted for inflation.</li>
      <li>In the circular flow model, income = output = expenditure.</li>
      <li>Injections add spending to the circular flow.</li>
      <li>Withdrawals remove spending from the circular flow.</li>
      <li>Equilibrium income occurs when injections equal withdrawals.</li>
      <li>Full employment income occurs when resources are fully used.</li>
      <li>Changes in injections and withdrawals affect national income.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

